.\" zlib-test.1 -- userland/packages/zlib.  MIT, see LICENSE in userland/packages.
.TH ZLIB-TEST 1 "2026-10-30" "zlib 1.2.13" "Amix add-on commands"
.SH NAME
zlib\-test \- check the installed zlib library on this machine
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B /opt/amix/bin/zlib\-test
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B zlib\-test
is linked against the installed
.B /opt/amix/lib/libz.a
and checks, on this machine:
.IP 1. 3
the
.B crc32
and
.B adler32
checksums of a fixed string against their known values, which catch a
byte-order mistake;
.IP 2. 3
a deflate and inflate round trip of four megabytes of mixed repeating and
pseudo-random data, compared byte for byte;
.IP 3. 3
inflating a stream another zlib produced.
.PP
It prints one line per check, with the version of zlib it is linked against,
and a verdict.
.SH EXIT STATUS
0 when every check passed, 1 otherwise.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR zlib (3)
